  },
  "kind": "statement",
  "title": "Affine schemes are quasi-affine",
  "statement": "If $U$ is affine, then $U$ is quasi-affine in the sense used in\n[lemma-nagata-quasi-affine-immersion-affine-space-exists]; in\nparticular that lemma applies to any $U\\to S$ of finite type with $U$\naffine.",
  "source": {
    "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-nagata-compactification/sk-prop-nagata-sketch-zmt/lemma-nagata-affine-finite-type-is-quasi-affine.md",
    "place": "node lemma-nagata-affine-finite-type-is-quasi-affine, order 186"
  },
  "stmt_deps": [
    "lemma-nagata-quasi-affine-immersion-affine-space-exists"
  ],
  "proof": [
    {
      "text": "The identity of $U$ realizes the canonical map\n$U\\to\\operatorname{Spec}\\Gamma(U,\\mathcal O_U)$ as an open immersion, and\n$U$ is quasi-compact. This is the defining quasi-affine property, and a\nfinite-type structure morphism is in particular locally of finite type.",
      "uses": [],
      "elementary": null
    }
  ],
